                                "sense_id": "6b17db61-cadf-3047-bd97-bd3fc4134148",
                                "text": "To begin with, Reynolds’ decompositional strategy invoking sub-skills such as various visual recognitional capacities (as in Marr’s theory of vision) seems to be an appeal to the so-called ‘unconscious’ processes that lead up to experience and eventually to belief."
                            },
